' 21 Fire count of a space transaction: one count for its settles and its plan.
'
' Source of Figure N11.5 in ../design.md (section N11.5). The figure restates
' Plan.rounds, Cx::rounds and open_plan of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/generic.rs and the settle loop of
' spaces/settle.rs (plan revision I-21, decision 49). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. A transaction starts with the count 0, and every fire of the
'      transaction adds 1, whoever makes it.
'   2. The settle before the plan stops at the cap. The transaction commits
'      its fires and re-issues the operation, which it has not inserted yet.
'   3. The plan opens only below the cap. A full transaction re-issues the
'      operation before the plan stages anything.
'   4. The settle after the plan continues the count. At the cap it re-issues
'      a settle job, which is a transaction of its own.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 21-transaction-fire-count.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 21-transaction-fire-count
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
title One fire count for each space transaction (I-21)

start
:run_with: bump the counter
the count of the transaction is 0; <<$rrs_substrate>>
:settle before the plan
(each fire adds 1 to the count); <<$rrs_agent>>
if (the settle reached the cap with a fire left?) then (yes)
  :commit the staged fires
  re-issue the operation (decision 43 keeps its order); <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (the count is FIRE_ROUND_CAP? (open_plan)) then (yes)
  :commit the fires of the settle
  re-issue the operation (its plan stages nothing); <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
:the plan: fires while the count stays below the cap; <<$rrs_agent>>
if (the plan re-issues?) then (yes)
  :commit the staged fires
  re-issue the operation; <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
:settle after the plan
(it continues the count); <<$rrs_agent>>
if (the settle reached the cap with a fire left?) then (yes)
  :commit, and re-issue a settle job
  (a transaction of its own, from the count 0); <<$rrs_reject>>
else (no)
endif
:commit: at most <latex>\mathrm{FIRE\_ROUND\_CAP} = 64</latex> fires; <<$rrs_effect>>
stop
@enduml
